# Build-time configuration for every deployment of the CRM.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle at build time, so
# they have to be present when the build runs. Keeping them here rather than in
# a host's dashboard means a fresh deploy is correct by default and cannot be
# built "unconfigured" by someone forgetting a setting — which is exactly what
# happened on the first Vercel build.
#
# Both values below are public by design: the publishable key is shipped to
# every browser that loads the app, and row level security, not the key, is the
# security boundary. Nothing secret belongs in this file.
#
# These MUST NOT be here, because they are real secrets — set them in the
# host's environment settings instead:
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY    bypasses RLS entirely
#   CRON_SECRET            /api/cron/tick returns 401 until it is set (fail-closed)
#   INTAKE_SIGNING_SECRET  verifies lead posts from the brand websites

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://knbsosxsfvqslpimiznl.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_zpOcpMhB-LlJ4poQdJezEQ_sL4UCCM0
